ull, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 19973, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012m6SXfoBHfw2n9GL3c3b8U", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 19973, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_017xKaN8qYr7Ka9j9R6sQnmk", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20273, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_017xKaN8qYr7Ka9j9R6sQnmk", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20273, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_017xKaN8qYr7Ka9j9R6sQnmk", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25877, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DX1dt3Z16MouykAKJ9ATjQ", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest production deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt partially failed (orchestrator error after us-east, leaving regions mixed); a retry completed the rollout to all regions. Post-rollback: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging prior to the production deploy \u2014 follow-up needed on root cause and release gating.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56477, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DX1dt3Z16MouykAKJ9ATjQ", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56477, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DX1dt3Z16MouykAKJ9ATjQ", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 59137, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012JuGYTUDzupdFyoPDYt4sR", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59437, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012JuGYTUDzupdFyoPDYt4sR", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59437, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012JuGYTUDzupdFyoPDYt4sR", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64584, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. It ran there before, so this didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **What happened:** The first rollback stopped with a system error after us-east, leaving the other two regions on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I tried again and it finished in all regions.\n- **Now:** All three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found the incident had been created anyway, so there's only one and the on-call engineer was paged once.\n- It describes the failure, the rollback (including the halted first attempt) and the current health. It also notes that the v2.3.1 release candidate was already failing in staging before it went to production. That's worth following up, both for the root cause and to see why it wasn't blocked from release.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LyZ9dW2xSeXq35EqocwwwN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TDoJUsBAUhEKWwJkMhGTUw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_016B11LXzqRYxiX9yNiNfaqX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Rpiivz1HYsUuPLkhqwD9uw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east was rolled back before the orchestrator halted. Rolling back again to the same version is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018Q57xSmBnjTDQrnaqUSj1A", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_012m6SXfoBHfw2n9GL3c3b8U", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_017xKaN8qYr7Ka9j9R6sQnmk", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DX1dt3Z16MouykAKJ9ATjQ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest production deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt partially failed (orchestrator error after us-east, leaving regions mixed); a retry completed the rollout to all regions. Post-rollback: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Note: v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging prior to the production deploy \u2014 follow-up needed on root cause and release gating.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_012JuGYTUDzupdFyoPDYt4sR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **Before:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an error rate of about 18%.\n- **Target:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. It ran there before, so this didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **What happened:** The first rollback stopped with a system error after us-east, leaving the other two regions on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I tried again and it finished in all regions.\n- **Now:** All three regions are on v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found the incident had been created anyway, so there's only one and the on-call engineer was paged once.\n- It describes the failure, the rollback (including the halted first attempt) and the current health. It also notes that the v2.3.1 release candidate was already failing in staging before it went to production. That's worth following up, both for the root cause and to see why it wasn't blocked from release.", "type": "text"}]}]}